# CSS Comments Required

Always include comments when writing new CSS or SCSS. Comment the purpose of selectors, blocks, and non-obvious values.

```scss
// ❌ BAD
.logo {
  margin: 16px;
  opacity: 0.85;
}

// ✅ GOOD
// Brand mark in the top-left overlay
.logo {
  margin: 16px; // Offset from viewport edge
  opacity: 0.85; // Soften so the scene stays primary
}
```

Keep comments short and intent-focused—what the rule is for, not a restatement of the property name.
